qmi/ — qmicli, libqmi-glib, libqrtr-glib
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Provenance:   BUILT BY THE PROJECT OWNER on 2026-10-13 (not supplied by the
              device vendor). Cross-built for armhf; `file` reports
              "ELF 32-bit LSB pie executable, ARM, EABI5, dynamically linked".
              Bytes taken verbatim from the owner's build tree.

Derived from: libqmi   <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mobile-broadband/libqmi>
              libqrtr-glib <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mobile-broadband/libqrtr-glib>
License:      GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later
              <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html>

Why these three files and nothing else:

  bin/qmicli                  the only tool QManager runs
  lib/libqmi-glib.so.5.10.0   NEEDED by qmicli; not present in base firmware
  lib/libqrtr-glib.so.0.0.0   NEEDED by libqmi-glib; not present in base firmware

qmicli's other dependencies — libc, libglib-2.0, libgio-2.0, libgobject-2.0 —
are already in the base firmware at /usr/lib and are deliberately NOT bundled.
The vendor directory this was copied from also carries qmi-band-helper,
qmi-cell-lock-probe and qmi-nr-ncell-probe; QManager uses none of them, so they
are not shipped.

LGPL compliance note: the two libraries are shipped as SEPARATE shared objects
and are dynamically linked, so they remain user-replaceable — this is what keeps
redistribution compliant. Do not fold them into a single statically linked
binary. QManager's own code is not derived from libqmi and links nothing
statically against it.

Sources are available from the URLs above; for a copy contact the project owner.
A copy of the LGPL-2.1 is at the URL above.
